 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Wind, cloud and rain, then growth for the revived land and the good land. The resurrection («كذلك نخرج الموتى») is not drawn. First-person «سقناه… فأنزلنا… نصرف» not used. STAGING v4: c1 (57): a dry desert by day with a few of its people (As-Sa'di: the dead land whose people nearly despaired). The wind on 57:4 and the people raise their hands in joy on 57:5 (both tafsirs: the creation rejoices at the good tidings); a cloud plate for the heavy clouds (57:12), the camera to the sky (57:13) and they look up (57:14); rain on the dead land from 57:17 to 57:24 (the water sent down), the land turns green on 57:20 (the plants brought out), a palm plate for the fruits and joy again on 57:24 (As-Sa'di: they rejoiced at His mercy). 57:25-29 (so will We bring out the dead): the resurrection is not drawn; the camera stays on the land. c2 (58): fields; the good land's plants come out on 58:3 (growth event, wheat plate); for the bad land (58:7-12) the wind blows and a single leaf plate undraws (scanty growth), the camera on the ground; believers come in on 58:16 and raise their hands on 58:17 (Al-Muyassar: people who thank Allah for His favours). FOR THE REVIEWER (review M8, accepted): the bad land of 58:7-12 is still shown on the same green wheat field; only the wind, falling leaves and a single leaf plate that undraws stand for its scanty growth, so the picture does not show bare ground."
 },
